Usage:
  Single cell:
    bin/geniex-bench --plugin {llama_cpp|qairt} --device {cpu|gpu|npu|hybrid|auto} \
                              -m <path> [options]

  Matrix (one process, shared geniex_init/deinit):
    bin/geniex-bench --matrix-file <path> [--output-json-dir <dir>] [shared options]

Required (single-cell mode):
  --plugin            llama_cpp | qairt
  --device            cpu | gpu | npu | hybrid | auto (default auto)
  -m, --model VALUE   either a filesystem path (.gguf or bundle dir) or
                      a model-manager id `org/repo[:quant]`. The id form
                      pulls via geniex_model_pull on first use and reuses
                      the cached copy thereafter. The manager's tokenizer
                      shadows --tokenizer-path; the manager's mmproj is
                      adopted ONLY when VLM is explicitly requested via
                      --vlm (single-cell) or the matrix `vlm` column. An
                      explicit --mmproj-path / matrix col 6 always wins.

Required (matrix mode):
  --matrix-file PATH  one cell per line, tab-separated:
                      cell_id<TAB>plugin<TAB>device<TAB>model_path_or_id[<TAB>tokenizer_path][<TAB>mmproj_path][<TAB>image_paths][<TAB>vlm]
                      column 4 is a model-manager id when it doesn't look
                      like a path (no leading '/' / drive prefix and at
                      least one '/'); otherwise it's used verbatim as a
                      filesystem path.
                      image_paths is comma-separated; vlm non-empty forces
                      VLM mode (QAIRT bundles without an mmproj)
                      lines starting with '#' are ignored

Optional (llama-bench-style names):
  -r, --repetitions N    default 5 (measured runs)
  -p, --n-prompt N       LLM prefill length (random token ids); default 512.
                         Mirrors `llama-bench -p N`: the bench tool fills N
                         positions with `rand() % vocab_size` (BOS at pos 0
                         when the model wants one) and feeds them via
                         input_ids, so `pp` is exactly N for every model.
                         Requires the plugin to implement
                         geniex_llm_get_model_info; the tool fails with a
                         clear error otherwise.
  -n, --n-gen N          tokens to generate per run; default 128
  -c, --ctx-size N       model n_ctx (0 = from model, default 0)
  -t, --threads N        generation threads (0 = SDK default)
  -ngl, --n-gpu-layers N llama_cpp layers to offload; overrides the
                         device alias default (-1 = all layers)
  --qairt-lib DIR        run against another QAIRT runtime (qairt): a QAIRT SDK
                         root or a flat folder of QNN libraries. Applies to the
                         whole run -- the QNN libraries load once per process.
  --spec-type TYPES      speculative type(s), comma-separated: draft-mtp,
                         draft-eagle3,draft-simple,ngram-simple,ngram-map-k,
                         ngram-map-k4v,ngram-mod,ngram-cache (llama_cpp)
  --draft-model PATH     draft/MTP GGUF for draft-* spec types (llama_cpp)
  --draft-tokens N       max draft tokens per step (0 = plugin default)
  --draft-min N          min draft tokens per step (0 = llama.cpp default)
  --draft-p-min F        min greedy draft probability (0 = llama.cpp default)
  --power-mode MODE      HTP power/clock-management mode, shared by qairt and
                         llama_cpp: low_power_saver, power_saver, high_power_saver,
                         low_balanced, balanced, high_performance,
                         sustained_high_performance, burst (default)
  --warmup N             default 1
  --no-warmup            equivalent to --warmup 0
  --temperature F        default 0.0
  --top-p F              default 0.0 (defers to the bundle's dialog.sampler.top-p,
                         then the plugin default, e.g. 0.95 for qairt/llama_cpp)
  --seed N               default 42; also seeds rand() for prompt ids
  --prompt-file PATH     opt out of random-ids prefill: read a UTF-8 prompt
                         from PATH and feed it via prompt_utf8 instead. The
                         only way to bench plugins that don't implement
                         geniex_llm_get_model_info. With this flag, reported
                         `pp` is the tokenizer's count, NOT --n-prompt.
                         For qairt, `pp` and prefill tok/s are reported over
                         the padded length ceil(pp/128)*128, matching the
                         engine's 128-token prefill chunking (#1194).
                         Under --accuracy only, a line that is exactly `---`
                         splits the file into several prompts; each runs on
                         its own KV cache, is marked `[sep ] prompt i/n` on
                         stdout and gets its own entry in the JSON `runs`
                         array. Every other mode feeds the file verbatim as
                         one prompt, `---` lines included: the segments differ
                         in length, so a tok/s median across them would mix
                         populations.
  --no-reset-between-runs
                         keep KV cache across measured runs (default is
                         to call geniex_llm_reset() before every run so
                         each repetition does the full prefill, matching
                         llama-bench semantics)
  --accuracy             accuracy mode: force a single run (--warmup 0
                         --repetitions 1) and print the generated text to
                         stdout, for eyeballing output quality rather than
                         speed. Overrides --warmup / --repetitions. Pair
                         with --prompt-file for a real prompt; the default
                         random-ids prefill produces meaningless text.
                         Each --prompt-file segment is run through the
                         bundle's own chat template before generation --
                         same templating `geniex infer` uses -- so pass the
                         raw user turn, not pre-templated text.
  --system-prompt TEXT   with --accuracy --prompt-file: system message added
                         ahead of the prompt in the chat template
  --think / --no-think  with --accuracy --prompt-file: enable_thinking for
                         the chat template (default: think)
  --logits               prefill-only raw-logits mode: run one forward pass
                         (geniex_llm_forward_logits, no decode loop) over N
                         random token ids (-p N, like the timing default) and
                         write every position's logits row ([n_tokens, vocab])
                         to the JSON report, for on-target accuracy metrics
                         (perplexity/MMLU/MMMU). Bypasses timing; --warmup/-r/-n
                         are ignored. Input is random ids only (the
                         forward-logits API takes input_ids, and the bench tool
                         has no tokenizer): --prompt-file is rejected with
                         --logits.
  --logits-last-only     with --logits, emit only the last token's logits row
                         instead of every position (next-token / MMLU scoring).
  --logits-top-n N       with --logits, emit only the top-N (token_id, logit)
                         pairs per row (default 20) to keep the JSON small;
                         the report records this truncation.

Optional (multimodal):
  --tokenizer-path PATH  explicit tokenizer file
  --mmproj-path PATH     multimodal projector — switches to VLM mode
  --vlm                  force VLM mode without an mmproj (QAIRT bundles)
  --image PATH           image input (VLM); may be passed multiple times
  --audio PATH           audio input (VLM); may be passed multiple times
  --device-id ID         override resolved device id (e.g. HTP0, GPUOpenCL)

Optional (output):
  --output-json PATH     (single-cell) write per-cell JSON report
  --output-md PATH       (single-cell) write per-cell Markdown row
  --output-json-dir DIR  (matrix) write <DIR>/<cell_id>.json per cell
  --cell-id ID           (single-cell) cell label used in reports

Optional (model manager — applied when -m / matrix col 4 is a model id):
  --mm-data-dir DIR      cache root for downloaded models;
                         default: $GENIEX_DATADIR or ~/.cache/geniex
  --hub NAME             auto | hf | aihub | modelscope | volces
                         (default auto). hf reads $GENIEX_HFTOKEN.
  --chipset SLUG         AI Hub chipset slug, e.g. qualcomm-snapdragon-x-elite
                         (only consumed when the resolved hub is aihub)
  --help / -h
